Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban gc: sweep stale gc-rm trash; SELECT abort
 log; one home-key reset

Follow-ups to PR #1982's exact-head review (t_01a1d3fd707849a7, review 5888112869):

- gc_task_scratch: a detached `.<id>.gc-rm-<hex>` tree whose rmtree failed was only warned
  about and then reported owner_unverified on every later run. Each run now sweeps those
  names (workspaces root and beside each candidate; never a symlink, only names GC mints)
  after the candidate SELECT and outside any write txn, and _report_unowned_scratch skips them.
- The candidate SELECT is back inside the try: an unreadable board logs
  "Scratch GC aborted ..." and returns 0 instead of raising.
- env_loader._home_key's memo moves to hermes_constants.resolved_home_str (same semantics: no
  expanduser, no normcase, missing paths not memoized), so reset_hermes_home_key_cache()
  clears it together with hermes_home_key's.
- Docs: the control socket's 30 s cached "no symlinked ancestor" pass (an ancestor swapped for
  a symlink is admitted for up to 30 s) in developer-guide gateway-internals.md, with a pointer
  in gateway/AGENTS.md.

Tests: RED on base (5 failures), GREEN:
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_trash_sweep.py (5),
tests/test_hermes_home_key_cache.py (TestOneResetForEveryHomeMemo).
Every test file referencing the changed functions (86 files, 1409 tests) passes.

